---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — StudioAPI" description="Terms of service for using the StudioAPI platform.">
  <main class="content">
    <div class="container-wide py-20 lg:py-28">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="display-2 mt-5">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated: 2026-08-08</p>

        <div class="docs-content mt-10">
          <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
          <p>By accessing or using StudioAPI, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you are using StudioAPI on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization.</p>

          <h2>2. API access and keys</h2>
          <p>API keys are personal to your account. You must keep them confidential and are responsible for all activity performed with them. StudioAPI stores only cryptographic hashes of keys and cannot recover a lost key.</p>

          <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to misuse the service, including attempting to exceed rate limits, reverse-engineering, reselling access outside your plan, or using the service in violation of applicable law or third-party source terms.</p>

          <h2>4. Data sources and licensing</h2>
          <p>StudioAPI aggregates data from third-party public sources. Each source has its own license and attribution requirements, which are documented per endpoint. You are responsible for complying with those requirements in your own use.</p>

          <h2>5. Billing and payments</h2>
          <p>Paid plans and credits are billed as described at the time of purchase. Unused credits are non-refundable except where required by law. Subscription renewals follow the cycle selected at checkout.</p>

          <h2>6. Availability</h2>
          <p>The service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. StudioAPI uses multi-source failover and caching to improve reliability, but does not guarantee uninterrupted availability of any individual source.</p>

          <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, StudioAPI is not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the service.</p>

          <h2>8. Termination</h2>
          <p>You may stop using StudioAPI at any time. StudioAPI may suspend or terminate access for violations of these terms or applicable law.</p>

          <h2>9. Changes</h2>
          <p>We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes will be announced on the site or by email.</p>

          <h2>10. Contact</h2>
          <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:hello@studioapi.dev">hello@studioapi.dev</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
